"# Terminology & Translation Memory Bindings: *Deforestation*, *Rainforest*, *Biodiversity*\n\n**Deliverable type:** Multilingual termbase (TBX) concept entries + translation memory (TMX) seed units\n**Date:** 2026-09-25 | **Languages:** EN + ES, FR, DE, ZH (plus PT, RU, AR, JA, and others as secondary bindings)\n**Authority sources:** FAO, UNFCCC, IPCC, CBD, EU law, ISO terminology standards\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThis report binds three high-frequency environmental terms into a standards-compliant terminology and translation memory package. For each term, it (a) fixes the **authoritative definition** from the relevant treaty or scientific body, (b) records the **standard target-language equivalents** used in official multilingual texts, (c) serializes the result as **TBX (ISO 30042) concept entries**, and (d) supplies **TMX 1.4b translation units** with example bilingual segments.\n\nThe most consequential finding for translators: **\"deforestation\" is defined differently by FAO vs. UNFCCC/IPCC** (human-induced vs. any cause), **\"rainforest\" has no single legal definition** and maps to different words per language (*selva* vs. *bosque* in Spanish; *forêt tropicale humide* vs. *forêt ombrophile* in French), and **\"biodiversity\" has a legally binding six-language definition in CBD Article 2** whose authentic texts are the gold standard for translation. These definitional divergences must be captured in termbase metadata, not flattened.\n\n---\n\n## Part 1 — Standards Framework Governing the Bindings\n\n### 1.1 Termbase side: TBX / ISO 30042\n\nTermBase eXchange (TBX) is the ISO 30042:2019 format (TBX 3.0, with 2021 Amendment 1 = TBX 3.1), superseding the older MARTIF (ISO 12200) [10][11]. It is **concept-oriented**: one `conceptEntry` per concept, containing one `langSec` per language, each containing one or more `termSec` per term [10][11]. Data categories attach per level:\n\n| Level | Typical data categories |\n|---|---|\n| Concept | `subjectField`, `definition`, `sourceStatement`, cross-references |\n| Language | language-specific notes, usage sources |\n| Term | `termType`, `partOfSpeech`, `grammaticalGender/Number`, `usageNote`, `geographicalUsage`, `administrativeStatus` (preferred / admitted / deprecated / superseded) |\n\nISO 26162-1:2019 codifies the same three-level data model for termbase design; ISO 26162-2:2019 specifies termbase software requirements (TBX/CSV import-export, fuzzy search, QA) [15]. ISO 1087:2019 supplies the underlying theory — the concept-oriented model in which one concept carries multiple designations across languages [14].\n\n### 1.2 Translation memory side: TMX 1.4b\n\nTMX (Translation Memory eXchange) 1.4b remains the current version (2003; stewardship passed from LISA to GALA; TMX 2.0 was never finalized) [12]. It is **segment-oriented**: `tu` (translation unit) → `tuv` (language variant) → `seg` (segment) [12]. Critically, **TMX carries no definitions, no term status, and no concept identity** — only aligned segment pairs plus tool metadata [12]. This is precisely why the termbase and TM must be bound as complementary resources: the termbase holds canonical term knowledge; the TM holds reusable translation evidence.\n\n### 1.3 Workflow standard\n\nISO 12616-1:2021 governs translation-oriented terminography: needs analysis from source texts → term extraction → research → recording → quality control → maintenance → use in translation, with minimum record contents (source/target terms, definition/context, grammatical data, subject field, source reference, date/author, status) [13]. The best practice is **terminology first, TM second**: build the termbase, enforce it via QA tooling, then populate the TM.\n\n---\n\n## Part 2 — Concept Entries: Definitions and Source Authority\n\n### 2.1 CONCEPT-001: `deforestation`\n\n**The definition depends on the authority — this must be recorded in the termbase:**\n\n| Authority | Definition | Key qualifier |\n|---|---|---|\n| **FAO (FRA 2020)** | \"The conversion of forest to other land use, regardless of whether it is human-induced or not\" [1] | Includes natural causes; implies long-term/permanent land-use change; temporary clearing followed by regeneration is *not* deforestation [1] |\n| **UNFCCC (Decision 11/CP.7, Marrakesh Accords)** | \"The direct human-induced conversion of forested land to non-forested land\" [2] | Direct human induction required; carried through REDD+ (Decision 1/CP.16) and UN-REDD [2][3] |\n| **IPCC (2006 GL Vol. 4 / 2019 Refinement)** | Same as UNFCCC: \"direct human-induced conversion of forested land to non-forested land\" [4] | Short form in SRCCL/AR6 glossaries: \"conversion of forest to non-forest\" [5] |\n| **EU (Reg. 2023/1115, EUDR)** | \"The conversion of forest to agricultural use, whether human-induced or not\" [6] | Narrower object (agricultural use) |\n\n**Termbase implication:** the English headword *deforestation* is one concept, but the definition field must be context-tagged (FAO / UNFCCC-REDD+ / EU legal). A REDD+ project document must translate the UNFCCC sense; an EUDR compliance text must use the EU sense.\n\n### 2.2 CONCEPT-002: `rainforest` / `tropical rainforest`\n\n**No treaty definition exists.** FAO does not formally define \"rainforest\" — it defines *forest* (land >0.5 ha, trees ≥5 m, canopy >10%) [1]; FAO's Global Ecological Zones classification includes a climatically delimited **\"Tropical rain forest\"** zone (very high, aseasonal rainfall ≥~1,800 mm, continuously warm) [17]. Scientific definitions are structural + climatic: Whitmore (1998) — evergreen, ≥30 m tall, rich in lianas/epiphytes, ~2,000–4,000 mm rainfall, no pronounced dry season; Richards (1996) — evergreenness, hygrophily, height, liana/epiphyte abundance, no single dominant species [16]. The term itself was coined in German as *tropischer Regenwald* by Schimper (1898) — meaning **German is the etymological source language** for this concept [16]. Temperate rainforest is defined separately (Alaback 1991) [16].\n\n### 2.3 CONCEPT-003: `biodiversity` / `biological diversity`\n\n**The only term of the three with a legally binding multilingual definition.** CBD Article 2 (\"Use of Terms\"), with six equally authentic UN-language versions [8][9]:\n\n| Language | Term | Definition (authentic text, abridged) |\n|---|---|---|\n| EN | **biological diversity** | \"the variability among living organisms from all sources including, inter alia, terrestrial, marine and other aquatic ecosystems and the ecological complexes of which they are part; this includes diversity within species, between species and of ecosystems\" [8] |\n| ES | **diversidad biológica** (short: *biodiversidad*) | \"la variabilidad de organismos vivos de cualquier fuente… comprende la diversidad dentro de cada especie, entre las especies y de los ecosistemas\" [8][9] |\n| FR | **diversité biologique** (short: *biodiversité*) | \"la variabilité des organismes vivants de toute origine… la diversité au sein des espèces et entre celles-ci ainsi que celle des écosystèmes\" [8][9] |\n| RU | **биологическое разнообразие** (short: *биоразнообразие*) | \"вариабельность живых организмов из всех источников…\" [8][9] |\n| ZH | **生物多样性** | \"所有来源的活的生物体中的变异性…包括物种内、物种之间和生态系统的多样性\" [8][9] |\n| AR | **التنوع البيولوجي** | \"تغاير الكائنات الحية من جميع مصادرها…\" [8][9] |\n\nThe three-component structure (within-species / between-species / ecosystem diversity) is preserved in all six authentic versions [8][9]. Note the Latinism *inter alia* is rendered \"entre otras cosas\" (ES), \"entre autres\" (FR), \"среди прочего\" (RU), \"除其他外\" (ZH), \"على سبيل المثال لا الحصر\" (AR) [8][9].\n\n---\n\n## Part 3 — TBX Concept Entries (Ready to Import)\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<tbx type=\"TBX-Core\" xml:lang=\"en\" xmlns=\"urn:iso:std:iso:30042:ed-3\">\n  <tbxHeader><!-- project metadata: domain 06 Forestry / 16 Biology, creation date, custodian --></tbxHeader>\n  <text><body>\n\n  <conceptEntry id=\"CONCEPT-001\">\n    <descrip type=\"subjectField\">06 Forestry / 6105 Forest destruction</descrip>\n    <descrip type=\"definition\">Permanent conversion of forest to other land use\n      (FAO, incl. natural causes) OR direct human-induced conversion of forested\n      land to non-forested land (UNFCCC/IPCC/REDD+).</descrip>\n    <descrip type=\"usageNote\">Definition varies by authority: FAO FRA counts any\n      cause; UNFCCC requires direct human induction; EU Reg. 2023/1115 limits the\n      object to conversion to agricultural use. Select definition per text type.</descrip>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"en\">\n      <termSec id=\"t1\">\n        <term>deforestation</term>\n        <termNote type=\"partOfSpeech\">noun</termNote>\n        <termNote type=\"termType\">fullForm</termNote>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n      </termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"es\">\n      <termSec id=\"t2\">\n        <term>deforestación</term>\n        <termNote type=\"partOfSpeech\">noun</termNote>\n        <termNote type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote>\n        <admin type=\"sourceStatement\">FAO/UNFCCC official ES; RAE-recognized\n          (variant: desforestación)</admin>\n      </termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"fr\">\n      <termSec id=\"t3\">\n        <term>déboisement</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"sourceStatement\">FAO/UNFCCC official FR</admin>\n      </termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t4\">\n        <term>déforestation</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">admittedTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">General/EU legal usage (Reg. (UE) 2023/1115)</admin>\n      </termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"de\">\n      <termSec id=\"t5\"><term>Entwaldung</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t6\"><term>Abholzung</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">= clearing/felling; do not use for the\n          land-use-change concept</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"zh\">\n      <termSec id=\"t7\"><term>毁林</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"sourceStatement\">FAO/UNFCCC/IPCC ZH texts</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"pt\">\n      <termSec id=\"t8\"><term>desmatamento</term>\n        <admin type=\"geographicalUsage\">BR</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t9\"><term>desflorestação</term>\n        <admin type=\"geographicalUsage\">PT / EU</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"ru\">\n      <termSec id=\"t10\"><term>обезлесение</term>\n        <admin type=\"sourceStatement\">FAO</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t11\"><term>сведение лесов</term>\n        <admin type=\"sourceStatement\">UNFCCC / REDD+</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n  </conceptEntry>\n\n  <conceptEntry id=\"CONCEPT-002\">\n    <descrip type=\"subjectField\">06 Forestry / 6103 Forest types; 16 Biology / ecology</descrip>\n    <descrip type=\"definition\">Evergreen, structurally complex forest (typically ≥30 m,\n      lianas and epiphytes abundant) of continuously warm climates with high, largely\n      aseasonal rainfall (~2,000–4,000+ mm; FAO GEZ threshold ≥~1,800 mm).</descrip>\n    <descrip type=\"usageNote\">No treaty definition; FAO defines \"forest,\" and\n      \"tropical rain forest\" appears as an ecological zone (GEZ). Distinguish\n      temperate rainforest (Alaback 1991). \"Jungle\" is colloquial — deprecated\n      in technical texts.</descrip>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"en\">\n      <termSec id=\"t1\"><term>rainforest</term>\n        <termNote type=\"termType\">fullForm</termNote></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t2\"><term>tropical rainforest</term>\n        <termNote type=\"termType\">entryTerm</termNote></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"es\">\n      <termSec id=\"t3\"><term>selva tropical</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">RAE: selva = bosque espeso; traditional word for\n          dense tropical forest (selva amazónica)</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t4\"><term>bosque tropical húmedo</term>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">FAO/forestry register; matches WWF biome\n          \"tropical moist broadleaf forests\"</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t5\"><term>jungla</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">Colloquial loanword</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"fr\">\n      <termSec id=\"t6\"><term>forêt tropicale humide</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t7\"><term>forêt ombrophile</term>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">Technical/phytosociological</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t8\"><term>forêt dense humide</term>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">Francophone forestry administration (ONF Guyane)</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"de\">\n      <termSec id=\"t9\"><term>(tropischer) Regenwald</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">Original Schimper (1898) coinage; subtypes:\n          Tieflandregenwald, Bergregenwald, Nebelwald (cloud forest),\n          Urwald (primary forest)</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"zh\">\n      <termSec id=\"t10\"><term>雨林</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t11\"><term>热带雨林</term>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">Standard in Chinese scientific literature;\n          distinct terms: 季雨林 (monsoon forest), 云雾林 (cloud forest)</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"pt\">\n      <termSec id=\"t12\"><term>floresta tropical úmida</term></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t13\"><term>floresta pluvial tropical</term></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n  </conceptEntry>\n\n  <conceptEntry id=\"CONCEPT-003\">\n    <descrip type=\"subjectField\">16 Biology / 1615 Biodiversity</descrip>\n    <descrip type=\"definition\">The variability among living organisms from all sources\n      including, inter alia, terrestrial, marine and other aquatic ecosystems and the\n      ecological complexes of which they are part; this includes diversity within\n      species, between species and of ecosystems. [CBD Art. 2]</descrip>\n    <descrip type=\"sourceStatement\">Convention on Biological Diversity, Article 2;\n      six equally authentic UN-language versions (Rio de Janeiro, 5 June 1992;\n      in force 29 Dec 1993).</descrip>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"en\">\n      <termSec id=\"t1\"><term>biological diversity</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">Legal/treaty form (CBD Art. 2)</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t2\"><term>biodiversity</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">admittedTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">Common short form; default in general prose</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"es\">\n      <termSec id=\"t3\"><term>diversidad biológica</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">Treaty form (Convenio sobre la Diversidad Biológica)</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t4\"><term>biodiversidad</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">admittedTerm-admn-sts</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"fr\">\n      <termSec id=\"t5\"><term>diversité biologique</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t6\"><term>biodiversité</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">admittedTerm-admn-sts</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"de\">\n      <termSec id=\"t7\"><term>biologische Vielfalt</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">Übereinkommen über die biologische Vielfalt</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t8\"><term>Biodiversität</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">admittedTerm-admn-sts</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"zh\">\n      <termSec id=\"t9\"><term>生物多样性</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin>\n        <admin type=\"usageNote\">Authentic CBD ZH text; itself means\n          \"biological diversity\"</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"ru\">\n      <termSec id=\"t10\"><term>биологическое разнообразие</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin></termSec>\n      <termSec id=\"t11\"><term>биоразнообразие</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">admittedTerm-admn-sts</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n    <langSec xml:lang=\"ar\">\n      <termSec id=\"t12\"><term>التنوع البيولوجي</term>\n        <admin type=\"administrativeStatus\">preferredTerm-admn-sts</admin></termSec>\n    </langSec>\n  </conceptEntry>\n\n  </body></text>\n</tbx>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Part 4 — TMX Translation Units (Seed Memory)\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<tmx version=\"1.4\">\n  <header creationtool=\"Termbind\" creationtoolversion=\"1.0\"\n          segtype=\"sentence\" o-tmf=\"tmx\" adminlang=\"en\"\n          srclang=\"en\" datatype=\"plaintext\"/>\n  <body>\n    <tu tuid=\"TM-001\" srclang=\"en\">\n      <prop type=\"x-domain\">environment-forestry</prop>\n      <prop type=\"x-client\">generic</prop>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"en\"><seg>Deforestation in the Amazon rainforest has\n        accelerated over the past decade.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"es\"><seg>La deforestación en la selva amazónica se ha\n        acelerado durante la última década.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"fr\"><seg>La déforestation dans la forêt amazonienne s'est\n        accélérée au cours de la dernière décennie.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"de\"><seg>Die Entwaldung im Amazonas-Regenwald hat sich im\n        vergangenen Jahrzehnt beschleunigt.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"zh\"><seg>过去十年，亚马逊雨林的毁林速度不断加快。</seg></tuv>\n    </tu>\n    <tu tuid=\"TM-002\" srclang=\"en\">\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"en\"><seg>Tropical rainforests are home to more than half\n        of the world's plant and animal species.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"es\"><seg>Las selvas tropicales albergan más de la mitad\n        de las especies de plantas y animales del mundo.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"fr\"><seg>Les forêts tropicales humides abritent plus de\n        la moitié des espèces végétales et animales de la planète.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"de\"><seg>Tropische Regenwälder beherbergen mehr als die\n        Hälfte der Pflanzen- und Tierarten der Erde.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"zh\"><seg>热带雨林孕育了地球上超过一半的动植物物种。</seg></tuv>\n    </tu>\n    <tu tuid=\"TM-003\" srclang=\"en\">\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"en\"><seg>The loss of biodiversity undermines ecosystem\n        services such as water purification and carbon sequestration.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"es\"><seg>La pérdida de biodiversidad socava servicios\n        ecosistémicos como la purificación del agua y el secuestro de carbono.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"fr\"><seg>La perte de biodiversité compromet des services\n        écosystémiques tels que la purification de l'eau et la séquestration\n        du carbone.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"de\"><seg>Der Verlust der Biodiversität untergräbt\n        Ökosystemleistungen wie die Wasserreinigung und die\n        Kohlenstoffbindung.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"zh\"><seg>生物多样性的丧失会削弱水净化、固碳等生态系统服务。</seg></tuv>\n    </tu>\n    <tu tuid=\"TM-004\" srclang=\"en\">\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"en\"><seg>Illegal logging remains one of the main drivers\n        of forest degradation.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"es\"><seg>La tala ilegal sigue siendo uno de los\n        principales factores de la degradación forestal.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"fr\"><seg>L'exploitation forestière illégale demeure l'un\n        des principaux facteurs de la dégradation des forêts.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"de\"><seg>Illegaler Holzeinschlag bleibt eine der\n        Hauptursachen der Walddegradation.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"zh\"><seg>非法采伐仍是造成森林退化的主要因素之一。</seg></tuv>\n    </tu>\n    <tu tuid=\"TM-005\" srclang=\"en\">\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"en\"><seg>Reforestation efforts must prioritize native\n        species to restore degraded habitats.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"es\"><seg>Las labores de reforestación deben priorizar\n        las especies nativas para restaurar los hábitats degradados.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"fr\"><seg>Les efforts de reboisement doivent privilégier\n        les espèces indigènes afin de restaurer les habitats dégradés.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"de\"><seg>Wiederaufforstungsmaßnahmen müssen heimische\n        Baumarten bevorzugen, um degradierte Lebensräume\n        wiederherzustellen.</seg></tuv>\n      <tuv xml:lang=\"zh\"><seg>再造林工作应优先采用乡土树种，以恢复退化的栖息地。</seg></tuv>\n    </tu>\n  </body>\n</tmx>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Part 5 — Consolidated Termbase (Quick-Reference)\n\n| English | Español | Français | Deutsch | 中文 | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| deforestation | deforestación | déboisement (FAO/UNFCCC) / déforestation (EU) | Entwaldung | 毁林 | Definition varies by authority [1][2][6] |\n| reforestation | reforestación | reboisement | Wiederaufforstung | 再造林 | replanting formerly forested land |\n| afforestation | forestación | boisement | Aufforstung | 造林 | planting on land never forested |\n| (tropical) rainforest | selva tropical / bosque tropical húmedo | forêt tropicale humide / forêt ombrophile | (tropischer) Regenwald | （热带）雨林 | No treaty definition [16][17] |\n| old-growth forest | bosque primario | forêt primaire | Urwald / Primärwald | 原始林 | |\n| biodiversity | biodiversidad | biodiversité | Biodiversität | 生物多样性 | Legal form: *diversidad biológica* / *diversité biologique* [8][9] |\n| ecosystem services | servicios ecosistémicos | services écosystémiques | Ökosystemleistungen | 生态系统服务 | |\n| carbon sink / sequestration | sumidero de carbono / secuestro de carbono | puits de carbone / séquestration du carbone | Kohlenstoffsenke / Kohlenstoffbindung | 碳汇 / 固碳 | |\n| habitat fragmentation | fragmentación del hábitat | fragmentation de l'habitat | Habitatfragmentierung | 栖息地破碎化 | |\n| illegal logging | tala ilegal | exploitation forestière illégale | illegaler Holzeinschlag | 非法采伐 | |\n| slash-and-burn agriculture | roza y quema | agriculture sur brûlis | Brandrodung | 刀耕火种 | ES variant: *agricultura itinerante* (FAO style) |\n| canopy | dosel | canopée | Kronendach | 林冠层 | |\n| endemic species | especies endémicas | espèces endémiques | endemische Arten | 特有物种 | |\n| protected area | área protegida | aire protégée | Schutzgebiet | 保护区 | |\n| sustainable forest management | gestión forestal sostenible | gestion durable des forêts | nachhaltige Waldbewirtschaftung | 可持续森林经营 | |\n\n---\n\n## Part 6 — Binding Rules, QA, and Maintenance\n\n**Terminology-first enforcement.** Per ISO 12616-1 workflow and industry practice, the termbase must be built and enforced via QA tooling (Xbench, Verifika, QA Distiller) *before* TM population; 75–99% fuzzy matches should be reviewed for terminology drift, not just length difference [13].\n\n**Disambiguation rules to encode:**\n- **Deforestation vs. forest degradation:** deforestation = land-use *change*; degradation = loss of forest condition within forest. The two terms must never be interchanged (UNFCCC treats them as separate reporting categories) [2][3].\n- **Reforestation vs. afforestation** (see table above) — a classic QA error.\n- **Selva vs. bosque (ES):** *selva* connotes dense, tropical, difficult-to-traverse forest (RAE); *bosque* is the neutral FAO \"forest\" [7]. Regional preference applies.\n- **\"Jungle\" (*jungla*, *jungle*)** is colloquial (via Hindi *jangal*) — deprecated in technical text [7].\n- **FR typography:** non-breaking space before `: ; ! ?` and inside guillemets « ».\n- **ZH numerals:** convert to 万-based units (10 million hectares → **1000万公顷**) — a frequent TM/QA failure; confirm Simplified vs. Traditional.\n- **Latin binomials** (*Bertholletia excelsa*) remain untranslated and italic; acronyms (REDD+, FSC, CITES, IUCN) retained, expanded once at first mention.\n\n**Fuzzy-match risk example:** \"Deforestation in the **Amazon**…\" vs. \"Deforestation in the **Congo Basin**…\" will match at very high similarity — region names, figures, and dates carry the factual risk in conservation reporting and must always be verified in fuzzy matches.\n\n**Maintenance:** record creation date, author, and administrative status per ISO 12616-1 minimum record contents [13]; use TBX `transacGrp` for transaction history and `administrativeStatus` transitions (preferred → superseded) when authorities update definitions — as FAO itself did between FRA 2000–2010 and FRA 2020 [1].\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n1. FAO, *Global Forest Resources Assessment 2020: Terms and Definitions* — https://www.fao.org/3/I8661EN/i8661en.pdf\n2. UNFCCC, Decision 11/CP.7 (Marrakesh Accords), FCCC/CP/2001/13/Add.1 — https://unfccc.int/resource/docs/cop7/13a01.pdf\n3. UNFCCC, Decision 1/CP.16 (Cancún Agreements / REDD+), FCCC/CP/2010/7/Add.1 — https://unfccc.int/resource/docs/2010/cop16/eng/07a01.pdf\n4. IPCC, *2006 IPCC Guidelines for National GHG Inventories*, Vol. 4 (AFOLU) — https://www.ipcc-nggip.iges.or.jp/public/2006gl/vol4.html\n5. IPCC, *Special Report on Climate Change and Land* (SRCCL, 2019), Glossary — https://www.ipcc.ch/srccl/\n6. Regulation (EU) 2023/1115 (EU Deforestation Regulation), Art. 2 — https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1115/oj\n7. RAE, *Diccionario de la lengua española* (deforestación, selva, bosque, jungla) — https://dle.rae.es/\n8. Convention on Biological Diversity, Article 2: Use of Terms — https://www.cbd.int/convention/articles/?a=cbd-02\n9. CBD, authentic texts in six UN languages — https://www.cbd.int/convention/text/\n10. ISO 30042:2019, *Management of terminology resources — TermBase eXchange (TBX)*\n11. TBX 3.0/3.1 specification and data-category registry — https://tbx.oscil.info\n12. TMX 1.4b specification, GALA — https://www.gala-global.org/tmx-14b\n13. ISO 12616-1:2021, *Translation-oriented terminography — Part 1*\n14. ISO 1087:2019, *Terminology work and terminology science — Vocabulary*\n15. ISO 26162-1/-2:2019, *Management of terminology resources — Terminology databases (Design / Computer applications)*\n16. Whitmore, *An Introduction to Tropical Rain Forests* (1998); Richards, *The Tropical Rain Forest*, 2nd ed. (1996); Schimper (1898); Alaback (1991)\n17. FAO, Global Ecological Zones (GEZ) classification\n18. ISO 17100:2015, *Translation services* (QA context)\n\n*Note: XML entries are seed bindings for import into a termbase/TM system; verify exact treaty wording against the linked authentic texts before legal or publication use.*"